#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# function_range

#% text
# `function_range(f, x, y)` gives the values of `f` over the reals as a condition on `y`; `function_range([f, cond], x, y)` on the part where `cond` holds.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# A rational function (parameters allowed) is decided by quantifier elimination of `exists(x, f == y)`; other functions of one variable by their extreme values on each interval of the domain (critical points, kinks of `abs`, ends, limits), so they are taken to be continuous there. A harmonic `c + a sin(w) + b cos(w)` gives `c - R <= y <= c + R`.

#% item
# A side without a bound drops out of the condition; `true` means every real value.

#% item
# A bound is closed only when a point of the domain takes the value; a limit that is approached but not taken (`exp` at `-inf`, `atan`, `tanh`, `1/(1 + x^2)` at infinity) gives an open bound. Every answer is checked against samples of the function; a function with jumps, or one the engine cannot analyse, leaves the call unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# A parabola:

#% cell
function_range(x^2, x, y)
#% output
#= y >= 0

#% text
# A cubic takes every value:

#% cell
function_range(x^3, x, y)
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# On an interval:

#% cell
function_range([x^2 + 1, -1 <= x and x <= 2], x, y)
#% output
#= 1 <= y and y <= 5

#% text
# A downward parabola:

#% cell
function_range(4 - x^2, x, y)
#% output
#= y <= 4

#% text
# A rational function and a function with a bounded range:

#% cell
[function_range(x/(1 + x^2), x, y), function_range(sin(x), x, y)]
#% output
#= [-1/2 <= y and y <= 1/2, -1 <= y and y <= 1]

#% text
# Bounds that are not attained are open:

#% cell
[function_range(exp(x), x, y), function_range(1/x, x, y), function_range(1/(1 + x^2), x, y), function_range(atan(x), x, y)]
#% output
#= [y > 0, y != 0, 0 < y and y <= 1, (-1/2)*pi < y and y < (1/2)*pi]

#% text
# Functions with a kink, a boundary or a periodic part:

#% cell
[function_range(abs(x), x, y), function_range(sqrt(x), x, y), function_range(log(x), x, y), function_range(sin(x) + cos(x), x, y)]
#% output
#= [y >= 0, y >= 0, true, -2^(1/2) <= y and y <= 2^(1/2)]

#% text
# A parameter:

#% cell
function_range(x^2 + a, x, y)
#% output
#= y >= a

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The ends are the minimum and the maximum:

#% cell
minimize([x^2 + 1, -1 <= x and x <= 2], x)
#% output
#= [1, [x -> 0]]

#% cell
maximize([x^2 + 1, -1 <= x and x <= 2], x)
#% output
#= [5, [x -> 2]]

#% text
# Sample values lie within the range `-1/2 <= y <= 1/2`:

#% cell
map(t => -1/2 <= t/(1 + t^2) and t/(1 + t^2) <= 1/2, [-10, -1, 0, 0.3, 2, 50])
#% output
#= [true, true, true, true, true, true]

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A function with jumps leaves the call unevaluated (its range is not an interval):

#% cell
function_range(floor(x), x, y)
#% output
#= function_range(floor(x), x, y)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `minimize`, `maximize`, `function_domain`
